  "dependencies": [
    "Fundamental theorem of calculus for polynomials: if P' = Q then P = ∫Q dx + constant",
    "Power rule for differentiation: (x^n)' = n·x^(n−1)",
    "Uniqueness of polynomial coefficients (distinct monomials are linearly independent over Q)"
  ],
  "argument": "Antiderivative: ∫(x³ − x)dx = x⁴/4 − x²/2 + C. Condition P(0) = 0 forces C = 0, giving P(x) = x⁴/4 − x²/2. Verification: P'(x) = 4·(x³/4) − 2·(x/2) = x³ − x ✓; P(0) = 0 − 0 = 0 ✓. P has rational coefficients, so P ∈ Q[x] ✓. Uniqueness: two polynomials with equal derivatives differ by a constant, and P(0) = 0 pins that constant to 0.",
  "unresolved_obligations": []
}

